cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Numerical Stability and Perturbation Behaviour in TF-IDF-Based
  Similarity Systems
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Matthew Maksymilian
    family-names: Miezaniec
    email: matthewmiezaniec1@gmail.com
    affiliation: King's College London
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Canon-Regularis/tfidf-stability-and-sensitivity
abstract: >-
  A self-contained implementation and analysis of a TF-IDF-based document
  similarity and ranking system, written to make the algebraic structure and
  perturbation behaviour of the pipeline explicit. The work treats ranking
  stability as a first-class object, characterising it through score-separation
  margin distributions, and isolates decision-level discontinuities introduced
  by deterministic tie-breaking rules. It comprises a normative pure-Python
  reference implementation and a bit-identical optimised C++20 evaluator, whose
  equivalence is enforced by the test suite.
keywords:
  - TF-IDF
  - information retrieval
  - cosine similarity
  - numerical stability
  - perturbation analysis
  - ranking stability
  - reproducibility
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-03-01'
